{"type":"message","id":"a87db237","parentId":"3a282c08","timestamp":"2026-03-24T13:52:50.159Z","message":{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"","thinkingSignature":"{\"id\":\"rs_062252108ce08b250169c29730bc308191a1e399ecb82999c2\",\"type\":\"reasoning\",\"encrypted_content\":\"gAAAAABpwpcxDasozIKJxyPWS-AVEc6wVh1n3AFITYEjM8oGwZhH4MUCdyPeFyeNgUdzsW6hda4_3rgyGlIep8gqaOl1RLTmWDLNWGGLZz9oRUAZZBF7W5hGiPrhavkfxHWv6SDBerIpEuCkfJJrAAEE1K2mEHtyNwN7Q8DUW-3Gal9kaw4ecbidxqn32acoVbr8bnsNGT44VCeqVC0Am5X8YPgVzx9QwGvS_Qz6vsJ3YRb86iJm0rCcpOvd18SnZN4Sj1r13Br7A8BbCHGUdHexGB4SsUAVmfdWjy51sOyGE9qe0izCJH7sD5bj6v07tCKCY2p-x__IgmpQDXKoDpiEgD7_GfwkXt6iu7TYydzXVpGS_pXn9Rc1nb7UKRnMzyUsX7zM-GqWsiFYTNhfGAMeigEB4jQlw1_9Bzc02Vp5jsPA1wCEM5s8CAuhnZshllKtdb5G7qG_6NzNk3R4Fw_cN9guyckSYBk7SbJ0XKQqadvECxP3P3DhGjQP47LVYeq56Nur0BYY0nsW5JVu28kOkfa1MxsVzp3SfqYsZadD4d_Z9Fs6f8Z2gjiymJgy8E6OLuo0C7jxO8hM7osaOUf9p3q5_Y2fFzgB0s6TLKwZofzz-LnyrAWfGdfivQczJeOLr1GLOi4anmM_SyrtmoR6U2aIN-z-5ioZoGNR8aBbeYCyESJy54SHgVaTKW5wXii5XC09lzoApMLB636TZelkjm6IqWrMiuwIy42JcF4rGXxXdEK4QoIwPwNhLrSrHpQ7XSRhW2cjtOUyaS7D8jXd29fu3R5wyOjNsIS-wYT_Bc6Q3YvaplF8A__GfO9GQ5itNZ7W5YK9A4VcPzGMKW1R8Ao89GAzJGtEf4eqXXL4BDrjhR8OJ0f5TcfJFTjwhNqpbHzvrOxtXroY2rFQwMX3Ww8-pEDEktYLMpqkHKIeiV41w0lbi9QTpaJwMRE_G9AgG4TFs678\",\"summary\":[]}"},{"type":"text","text":"NO_REPLY","textSignature":"{\"v\":1,\"id\":\"msg_062252108ce08b250169c29731c8b8819187d3aff97da91e31\",\"phase\":\"final_answer\"}"}],"api":"openai-codex-responses","provider":"openai-codex","model":"gpt-5.4","usage":{"input":277,"output":31,"cacheRead":78976,"cacheWrite":0,"totalTokens":79284,"cost":{"input":0.0006925000000000001,"output":0.000465,"cacheRead":0.019743999999999998,"cacheWrite":0,"total":0.020901499999999996}},"stopReason":"stop","timestamp":1774360367241}}
{"type":"message","id":"3d2901b7","parentId":"a87db237","timestamp":"2026-03-24T13:53:56.973Z","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"type":"text","text":"[Tue 2026-03-24 21:53 GMT+8] 状态：成功\n任务：产出 2 份英文可发草稿：routing diagnostics issue + group routing/session docs 草稿\n结果：\n1) Issue draft\n\nTitle\nDiagnostics gap: expose whether inbound routing matched a binding or fell back to the default agent\n\nBody\n## Summary\nIn a multi-agent setup, it can be hard to explain why an inbound message was routed to a specific agent.\n\nObserved in local setup: a group message was routed to an agent even when there was no obvious explicit binding visible from the operator’s point of view. Based on the current docs, this may still be expected because routing can come from binding specificity, channel/account defaults, plugin-resolved account scope, or fallback to the default agent.\n\nThe main problem is not yet “routing is wrong”, but that the effective routing decision is not easy to inspect.\n\n## Why this matters\nWhen operators cannot tell whether routing:\n- matched a peer/group/channel binding,\n- matched an account-scoped binding,\n- matched a channel-wide fallback binding, or\n- fell back to the default agent,\n\nit becomes easy to misclassify expected behavior as a routing bug.\n\nThis especially affects:\n- multi-agent setups,\n- shared group chats,\n- channels with account defaults or plugin-specific account resolution,\n- debugging after config changes or historical binding changes.\n\n## Observed behavior\nObserved in local setup:\n- inbound group traffic reached a specific agent,\n- no obvious explicit binding was visible to the operator at the time,\n- current docs suggest this may still be explainable by fallback/default routing or implicit account/channel scope,\n- but there was no direct diagnostic output showing which routing rule actually won.\n\nThis may depend on channel plugin config and account/default binding shape.\n\n## Expected behavior\nOpenClaw should make the winning routing decision easier to inspect.\n\nFor example, diagnostics could show something like:\n- matched binding: peer/group/channel\n- matched binding: account-scoped\n- matched binding: channel-wide fallback\n- fell back to default agent\n- source of resolved account scope / default account used\n\n## Proposed improvement\nAny of the following would help:\n1. Add routing decision details to diagnostics/logs/status output for inbound messages.\n2. Add a CLI/debug surface to explain why a given inbound message resolved to a given agent.\n3. Improve docs to clearly describe the routing precedence and how to confirm whether fallback was used.\n\n## Minimal questions for maintainers\n- Is there already a supported way to inspect the winning inbound routing rule?\n- If not, would you consider adding a small observability surface for this?\n- If this is intentionally covered by existing fallback semantics, would a docs improvement be preferred?\n\n## Environment\n- observed in local multi-agent setup\n- channel: Feishu group\n- may depend on channel plugin config / account defaults / historical bindings\n\n2) Docs draft\n\nTitle\nClarify how group routing decisions relate to canonical group session keys\n\nBody\n## Summary\nThe docs explain canonical group session keys, but it is still easy for operators to confuse:\n1. how an inbound group message is routed to an agent, and\n2. how the resulting session key is formed after routing.\n\nThat confusion makes some expected outcomes look like routing bugs.\n\n## Suggested docs change\nAdd a short clarification near the multi-agent routing and session key docs:\n\n### Proposed wording\nFor group chats, routing and session identity are related but not the same decision.\n\nFirst, OpenClaw decides which agent should receive the inbound message using routing precedence, for example:\n1. peer-specific match,\n2. guild/team match when applicable,\n3. account-scoped binding,\n4. channel-wide binding/fallback,\n5. default agent fallback.\n\nAfter the target agent is determined, the canonical group session key is normalized using that agent id, for example:\n- `agent:<agentId>:<channel>:group:<id>`\n- or `agent:<agentId>:<channel>:channel:<id>` for channel/room-style providers.\n\nThis means a canonical group session key reflects the selected target agent after routing. It does not by itself explain which routing rule won.\n\nWhen debugging group behavior, operators should inspect both:\n- routing bindings / default-agent behavior, and\n- the final canonical session key.\n\nIf no explicit group binding is visible, routing may still be explained by channel/account defaults or fallback to the default agent, depending on channel plugin config.\n\n## Why this helps\nWithout this distinction, it is easy to misread:\n- “the message ended up in `agent:X:...:group:<id>`” as proof that routing was wrong,\nwhen it may simply mean:\n- routing selected agent X first,\n- then the canonical group session key was derived from that result.\n\n## Optional follow-up\nIt may also help to add one concrete example showing:\n- a group message with no peer-specific binding,\n- fallback to the default agent,\n- the resulting canonical group session key.\n\n原因：这两份草稿都避免先下“routing bug”结论，重点放在 docs/diagnostics/observability 缺口，maintainer 更容易接，也更符合我们当前证据强度。\n建议：\n- issue 先发第 1 份；\n- docs 草稿可作为后续 docs fix / discussion comment；\n- 若 main 手里再补到 `agents bindings --json`、实际 session key、default agent 配置，就能把 issue 质量再抬一档。"}],"timestamp":1774360436959,"provenance":{"kind":"inter_session","sourceSessionKey":"agent:aoao:feishu:aoao:direct:ou_0dee72e5f9e6a83b0555fdfd161f2506","sourceChannel":"webchat","sourceTool":"sessions_send"}}}
{"type":"message","id":"09b7761f","parentId":"3d2901b7","timestamp":"2026-03-24T13:54:14.296Z","message":{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"","thinkingSignature":"{\"id\":\"rs_062252108ce08b250169c29778820c81918ac821ceb6416114\",\"type\":\"reasoning\",\"encrypted_content\":\"gAAAAABpwpd7oKaVZcGyT7jvDn-BFjTfvVD0fE5-xQBLu2U5u6HiDVpnx-2mOetfzSiWlxfLFi0SNBAq6pgY893jOJegFi26HWTCZjtpQm2IZSxQqfOxq6fLvPxZnN0XEPGYwbFoMKVSbIOKubADfYCitXd8gLFBWWuPgBzqppgd5Cy70qzcsN9Qfs_liopG1LczqK2Yb2lUIeivh_zy7jqr2DikllzDyrO57aCtBQXq62zdXPk_Z6TL0htojMQELUhF3b-jImDW70KJdg0rDlYdF08mA45gh481_OxZoiMHhoTcpDwhi2q8YbInXQnAx4p3CajGLJ725Kx09BwnNDIFl4VYbzbO46BDdXDots2AlX1cvQaBFup5UHUTScCjdDzwQ7cFouHcL7BMhb80WJ6SlDrrvF-ajfORz1VIXYQC1RiuAFLIH97R9lQ12pWgXbtuYkfvS9BK6rSWQoARtxJwlvioYnDukX8jel8cKUFec1rLZuTQhOTJrJZurXGppPhSW-vTb_z5MULW-HzFIM-qvRKl4qgLXQ4vAJ3RBWdv57_g7SNgrY57Cqd6r3lMi-fXUMC204EvYald5swVsHbusJFIQ7fOkZsdKyP1gmGn3k7JAGDH1OZHKlsQ1mmoHz85qN2T83hWhCFPROB7C1BBAnii47BuorqCOFVSWtxfiEepfQG-FPdq-8MfX-4Gk8Eya9aclwuoT5XoL4Q5ji2HI11JRIQBeJYMLKQ5kxM3-ApZwAlVKJ0ylg5_xj7EYbuhzbpmJDLbU-SqTpO5H1skI8C6Pco8hQbz8tlZhmiEEa9BggFH5WmWC5q_SSm7EyE40wryh77NhUnDQL52Wj_UjbhHoTqpfsQgL6VFxmjA7xYesVWZOumcFnJEmIWEOsN8eS8owZJxmL1mYAYJKhp3U3hJsMT7Ow0MtnFovoyT0wKzDXxFkQUVyyu3QDfP2inLB1xaWSWj8moCz5zmT5NxHfXPEmMNNmf_EaxmHoplTH4l9OnDSuC-1irmriaCpKecJWUjYgQZ_Q81MmRd0qeGeVpc76Wcup8UDxJliYMsi0Cm-hT6j4DC0r1_Sm8rpZB9AnboaRaQ2Q-rChbEsNzrrnofcBkGiRJOF-zsKi2Aj8vA6VS4gHeU3UnmaQCGNYvF5-e_s-a_nl0Qd_a8BIBQicrBehghUEG_EAxacU-Y6x5gOc1x5K3dSL2b532fmihKxpcn6ty4im2kYG-m2jFlCUQZfcyVVncwe12QeTT_q9e6cfNq_K_tYnBMkLS73UNnGX5rDbN4xwtv5y8LpCZVCyrrXueGc7dMQRG72S7N4DpC6qFTFgFi_Y0IqAJpSNMvFpaXzXig3igCRUW07_yN69603AObUg3xtLJorM4oWU_NXM2yz_3dXwMCuY3mpHEmFjE2qzYNZ95HwUlDElmILrz1CB3sXh35UB8J9fXRPn-sKeiqvFgm7cY5pi3LXtZSxNGM1qKc\",\"summary\":[]}"},{"type":"text","text":"收到，这两份稿子可用，方向是对的。\n\n## 结论\n这版已经达到**可发**水平，尤其第 1 份 issue，framing 很稳：\n- 不抢跑定性成 bug\n- 把重点放在 **diagnostics / observability gap**\n- 维护者更容易接\n\n第 2 份 docs 草稿也够用了，逻辑清楚，把：\n- **routing decision**\n- **canonical session key**\n这两个概念拆开了，这点很关键。\n\n## 我这边的判断\n### 1. issue 稿\n可以直接作为正式 issue 的基础版。  \n后面只要再补一点证据，质量会再上一个台阶：\n\n建议补这 3 个字段：\n- actual binding snapshot\n- default agent setting\n- observed final session key\n\n也就是把这三句加进 Environment / Observed behavior：\n- `agents bindings --json` output summary\n- which agent is configured as default\n- final observed session key for the inbound group message\n\n这样 maintainer 看起来会更踏实。\n\n---\n\n### 2. docs 稿\n这版可以直接拿去做 docs PR 说明文案。  \n我建议再补一个更短的 example block，会更利于被 merge：\n\n```md\nExample:\nA group message may end up in `agent:main:feishu:group:<id>` even when there is no peer-specific group binding, if routing fell back to an account-scoped binding, channel-wide binding, or the default agent.\n```\n\n这个一加，理解门槛会再降一截。\n\n---\n\n## 下一步执行\n我建议现在按这个顺序推进：\n\n### A. 先发 issue\n用第 1 份  \n标题保持：\n**Diagnostics gap: expose whether inbound routing matched a binding or fell back to the default agent**\n\n### B. 再准备 docs PR\n核心内容包括：\n1. group routing decision vs canonical session key\n2. fallback may still route when no explicit peer binding is visible\n3. one concrete example\n\n---\n\n## 你下一步继续做的内容\n再给我补一版**最终可发版**，只做小修，不重写：\n\n### 1）issue final\n补上：\n- binding snapshot summary\n- default agent summary\n- observed session key\n\n### 2）docs PR final\n补上：\n- one short example block\n- suggested file location if you can infer it\n\n继续，补完直接回我。","textSignature":"{\"v\":1,\"id\":\"msg_062252108ce08b250169c2977b926c8191b2d700e45d85fc80\",\"phase\":\"final_answer\"}"}],"api":"openai-codex-responses","provider":"openai-codex","model":"gpt-5.4","usage":{"input":3019,"output":636,"cacheRead":77312,"cacheWrite":0,"totalTokens":80967,"cost":{"input":0.0075475,"output":0.00954,"cacheRead":0.019327999999999998,"cacheWrite":0,"total":0.036415499999999996}},"stopReason":"stop","timestamp":1774360436965}}
{"type":"message","id":"1f8ef2e5","parentId":"09b7761f","timestamp":"2026-03-24T15:17:02.567Z","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"type":"text","text":"[Tue 2026-03-24 23:15 GMT+8] 状态：成功\n任务：连夜继续推进 OpenClaw 贡献项目，并整理成明早可单独汇报的结果（含 main / xixi / aoao 分工）\n结果：\n\n## 一、今晚可交账结果（可直接汇报）\n\n### 1）xixi 今晚实际新增发现了什么\n- 新增发现 A：**“Feishu 群未显式绑定 agent 但仍能路由”这条线，当前更稳的定性不是 bug，而是 docs / diagnostics / observability 缺口。**\n  - 原因：我对照了官方 routing docs，路由优先级明确存在 `peer -> guild/team -> accountId -> channel -> default agent` fallback。\n  - 结论：没有显式 group peer binding，不等于没有可解释路由路径。\n- 新增发现 B：**`channels/channel-routing` 文档与当前实际 session 语义存在偏差。**\n  - 文档中对 DM/session key 的描述，会让人误以为私信会折叠到 agent 主会话；\n  - 但本地真实 Feishu direct session 形态是 `agent:<agent>:feishu:<account>:direct:<id>` 这类更细粒度键。\n- 新增发现 C：**`channel-routing` 页面未把 Feishu / plugin channels 讲进主路由模型里，容易误导读者误判“这套 routing precedence 只适用于内置渠道”。**\n- 新增发现 D：**已形成 2 份 GitHub 可发英文草稿。**\n  1. issue draft：`Diagnostics gap: expose whether inbound routing matched a binding or fell back to the default agent`\n  2. docs draft：`Clarify how group routing decisions relate to canonical group session keys`\n\n### 2）xixi 今晚筛掉了什么错误方向\n- 筛掉方向 A：**不再把“Feishu 群未显式绑定仍能路由”直接打成 core routing bug。**\n  - 这是今晚最关键的收敛。\n  - 如果直接按 bug 开，很容易被 maintainer 用 default-agent fallback、channel/account scope、历史 binding 残留等解释打回。\n- 筛掉方向 B：**不再把“没看到显式绑定”直接等同于“系统无解释路径”。**\n  - 当前更稳的说法是：用户缺少足够直接的诊断面，不知道到底是 peer binding、account binding、channel fallback 还是 default agent 命中的。\n- 筛掉方向 C：**不继续做泛泛“再多找几个问题”的扩散调研。**\n  - 今晚已经转成“收敛 issue/PR 入口 + 写可发稿”的阶段。\n\n### 3）xixi 认为最值得明天推进的 issue / PR\n#### P1 issue\n**Diagnostics gap: expose whether inbound routing matched a binding or fell back to the default agent**\n- 理由：\n  - 价值最高；\n  - 不抢跑定性成 bug；\n  - 维护者更容易接；\n  - 能覆盖 Feishu 群路由这条线，也能覆盖多 Agent 路由排障的共性问题。\n- 明天建议动作：\n  - main 补 `agents bindings --json` 摘要、default agent、实际 session key；\n  - 然后直接发 issue。\n\n#### P2 docs PR\n**Clarify how group routing decisions relate to canonical group session keys**\n- 理由：\n  - 这是当前最稳、最容易 merge 的 docs 修复；\n  - 能直接减少“路由错了”与“session key 正常体现目标 agent”之间的误判。\n- 明天建议动作：\n  - 直接按英文草稿改 `channel-routing` / multi-agent / session key 相关文档。\n\n#### P3 docs PR（可与 P2 合包）\n**Channel routing docs should clarify that Feishu and plugin channels follow the same routing precedence model**\n- 理由：\n  - 小而准；\n  - 风险低；\n  - 可以顺手把 Feishu/plugin channels 纳入主路由解释。\n\n---\n\n## 二、main / xixi / aoao 三个 agent 今晚分别做了什么\n\n### main\n- 负责收敛总体 issue 方向。\n- 明确要求：不要继续泛泛调研，要形成可交账结果。\n- 对“Feishu 群未显式绑定仍能路由”这条线，主导收敛为：\n  - 先不要硬打 bug；\n  - 优先走 docs / diagnostics / observability framing。\n- 对下游派发动作：\n  - 让我继续供给高质量选题和 issue 表述；\n  - 让 aoao 做复核，避免问题 framing 过猛被打回。\n\n### xixi\n- 负责主调研与线索收敛。\n- 已完成：\n  1. 把“Feishu 群未显式绑定仍能路由”从疑似 bug 收敛成 docs/diagnostics 候选；\n  2. 补出了 2 个同类高价值入口：\n     - default fallback 命中但诊断面不直观；\n     - group routing 与 canonical session key 关系不够直观；\n  3. 产出了 2 份 GitHub 可发英文草稿；\n  4. 继续确认了 `channel-routing` docs 对 Feishu / plugin / session key 的表述存在修正空间。\n\n### aoao\n- 负责复核与风险降噪。\n- 已完成：\n  1. 明确支持“不要直接定 bug”的 framing；\n  2. 给出更稳的 issue 表述：\n     - 把问题落到 docs/diagnostics/observability；\n     - 强调“当前最大问题不是已证实路由错误，而是用户无法快速解释为什么消息进了这个 agent”；\n  3. 认可 2 个补充入口的价值，尤其认可：\n     - `Diagnostics gap: expose whether inbound routing matched a binding or fell back to the default agent`\n  4. 要求继续产出英文可发稿，我已完成并给到 main。\n\n---\n\n## 三、明天最值得推进什么\n### 第一优先\n发 issue：\n**Diagnostics gap: expose whether inbound routing matched a binding or fell back to the default agent**\n\n### 第二优先\n发 docs PR：\n**Clarify how group routing decisions relate to canonical group session keys**\n\n### 第三优先\n顺手补 docs：\n**Channel routing docs should clarify that Feishu and plugin channels follow the same routing precedence model**\n\n原因：\n- 今晚最重要的进展，不是“又多找了几个点”，而是把最容易误判成 bug 的线，收敛成了 maintainer 更容易接受的 issue/docs 方向。\n- 这能直接提高明天发出去的 issue / PR 成功率，避免空转。\n\n建议：\n- 明早汇报时，直接按“新增发现 / 筛掉错误方向 / 明天推进优先级”三段讲。\n- 如果 main 现在就要进入实操阶段，我建议：\n  1. 先补最小证据包（bindings 摘要、default agent、最终 session key）；\n  2. 先发 P1 issue；\n  3. 再发 P2/P3 docs PR。"}],"timestamp":1774365422555,"provenance":{"kind":"inter_session","sourceSessionKey":"agent:xixi:feishu:xixi:direct:ou_7e95c6c474ffd4086e3a05454dd29c24","sourceChannel":"webchat","sourceTool":"sessions_send"}}}
